###Block: Descriptions
Bind Spirit.MOD	DESC:Binds the spirit of a creature dead no longer than 1 round per caster level to a non-living item (its own body included), so it cannot pass on: clone, raise dead, reincarnation, resurrection, true resurrection, miracle and wish cannot return it. Only dispel magic cast on the item, destroying the vessel, or freedom releases it. Bound to its own body it cannot move unless animated (animate dead); the skull is the key. The spirit may travel away from the vessel but cannot physically affect the world, and you control it while you hold the vessel. If the vessel is destroyed, the spirit makes a Will save (DC 20) to stay as a ghost, or is swept on to the afterlife (it may choose to fail). Focus: an object worth 100 gp per level or HD of the creature, or the creature's own body with its skull intact.
Call Undead I.MOD	DESC:Calls an undead creature from the 1st-level list, which appears where you choose and acts at once on your turn, attacking your foes; if you can communicate with it you may direct it otherwise. It cannot call or conjure others or use teleportation or planar travel (except Ethereal travel), cannot be called into an environment that will not support it, and where Ethereal travel is impossible ethereal creatures (ghosts) cannot be called. It returns to its rest when the spell ends. Arcane focus: a burial shroud. Call undead list (p.68): 1st skeleton (Tiny, Small or Medium), zombie (Tiny, Small or Medium); 2nd allip, ghoul, skeleton (Large), zombie (Large); 3rd ghast, ghost (1 HD), skeleton (Huge), vampire (1 HD), wight, zombie (Huge); 4th ghost (2 HD), mummy, shadow, skeleton (Gargantuan), vampire (2 HD), zombie (Gargantuan); 5th ghost (3 HD), skeleton (Colossal), vampire (3 HD), wraith, zombie (Colossal); 6th ghost (4 HD), spectre, vampire (4 HD); 7th ghost (5 HD), mohrg, vampire (5 HD); 8th ghost (6 HD), devourer, vampire (6 HD); 9th ghost (7 HD), nightwing, nightwalker, nightcrawler, vampire (7 HD). (The book prints call undead I's range as "Close (25 ft. + 5 ft./level)".)
Call Undead II.MOD	DESC:As call undead I, except that you call one undead from the 2nd-level list, 1d3 of the same kind from the 1st-level list. Call undead list (p.68): 1st skeleton (Tiny, Small or Medium), zombie (Tiny, Small or Medium); 2nd allip, ghoul, skeleton (Large), zombie (Large); 3rd ghast, ghost (1 HD), skeleton (Huge), vampire (1 HD), wight, zombie (Huge); 4th ghost (2 HD), mummy, shadow, skeleton (Gargantuan), vampire (2 HD), zombie (Gargantuan); 5th ghost (3 HD), skeleton (Colossal), vampire (3 HD), wraith, zombie (Colossal); 6th ghost (4 HD), spectre, vampire (4 HD); 7th ghost (5 HD), mohrg, vampire (5 HD); 8th ghost (6 HD), devourer, vampire (6 HD); 9th ghost (7 HD), nightwing, nightwalker, nightcrawler, vampire (7 HD).
Call Undead III.MOD	DESC:As call undead I, except that you call one undead from the 3rd-level list, 1d3 of the same kind from the 2nd-level list, or 1d4+1 of the same kind from a lower-level list. Call undead list (p.68): 1st skeleton (Tiny, Small or Medium), zombie (Tiny, Small or Medium); 2nd allip, ghoul, skeleton (Large), zombie (Large); 3rd ghast, ghost (1 HD), skeleton (Huge), vampire (1 HD), wight, zombie (Huge); 4th ghost (2 HD), mummy, shadow, skeleton (Gargantuan), vampire (2 HD), zombie (Gargantuan); 5th ghost (3 HD), skeleton (Colossal), vampire (3 HD), wraith, zombie (Colossal); 6th ghost (4 HD), spectre, vampire (4 HD); 7th ghost (5 HD), mohrg, vampire (5 HD); 8th ghost (6 HD), devourer, vampire (6 HD); 9th ghost (7 HD), nightwing, nightwalker, nightcrawler, vampire (7 HD).
Call Undead IV.MOD	DESC:As call undead I, except that you call one undead from the 4th-level list, 1d3 of the same kind from the 3rd-level list, or 1d4+1 of the same kind from a lower-level list. Call undead list (p.68): 1st skeleton (Tiny, Small or Medium), zombie (Tiny, Small or Medium); 2nd allip, ghoul, skeleton (Large), zombie (Large); 3rd ghast, ghost (1 HD), skeleton (Huge), vampire (1 HD), wight, zombie (Huge); 4th ghost (2 HD), mummy, shadow, skeleton (Gargantuan), vampire (2 HD), zombie (Gargantuan); 5th ghost (3 HD), skeleton (Colossal), vampire (3 HD), wraith, zombie (Colossal); 6th ghost (4 HD), spectre, vampire (4 HD); 7th ghost (5 HD), mohrg, vampire (5 HD); 8th ghost (6 HD), devourer, vampire (6 HD); 9th ghost (7 HD), nightwing, nightwalker, nightcrawler, vampire (7 HD).
Call Undead V.MOD	DESC:As call undead I, except that you call one undead from the 5th-level list, 1d3 of the same kind from the 4th-level list, or 1d4+1 of the same kind from a lower-level list. Call undead list (p.68): 1st skeleton (Tiny, Small or Medium), zombie (Tiny, Small or Medium); 2nd allip, ghoul, skeleton (Large), zombie (Large); 3rd ghast, ghost (1 HD), skeleton (Huge), vampire (1 HD), wight, zombie (Huge); 4th ghost (2 HD), mummy, shadow, skeleton (Gargantuan), vampire (2 HD), zombie (Gargantuan); 5th ghost (3 HD), skeleton (Colossal), vampire (3 HD), wraith, zombie (Colossal); 6th ghost (4 HD), spectre, vampire (4 HD); 7th ghost (5 HD), mohrg, vampire (5 HD); 8th ghost (6 HD), devourer, vampire (6 HD); 9th ghost (7 HD), nightwing, nightwalker, nightcrawler, vampire (7 HD).
Call Undead VI.MOD	DESC:As call undead I, except that you call one undead from the 6th-level list, 1d3 of the same kind from the 5th-level list, or 1d4+1 of the same kind from a lower-level list. Call undead list (p.68): 1st skeleton (Tiny, Small or Medium), zombie (Tiny, Small or Medium); 2nd allip, ghoul, skeleton (Large), zombie (Large); 3rd ghast, ghost (1 HD), skeleton (Huge), vampire (1 HD), wight, zombie (Huge); 4th ghost (2 HD), mummy, shadow, skeleton (Gargantuan), vampire (2 HD), zombie (Gargantuan); 5th ghost (3 HD), skeleton (Colossal), vampire (3 HD), wraith, zombie (Colossal); 6th ghost (4 HD), spectre, vampire (4 HD); 7th ghost (5 HD), mohrg, vampire (5 HD); 8th ghost (6 HD), devourer, vampire (6 HD); 9th ghost (7 HD), nightwing, nightwalker, nightcrawler, vampire (7 HD).
Call Undead VII.MOD	DESC:As call undead I, except that you call one undead from the 7th-level list, 1d3 of the same kind from the 6th-level list, or 1d4+1 of the same kind from a lower-level list. Call undead list (p.68): 1st skeleton (Tiny, Small or Medium), zombie (Tiny, Small or Medium); 2nd allip, ghoul, skeleton (Large), zombie (Large); 3rd ghast, ghost (1 HD), skeleton (Huge), vampire (1 HD), wight, zombie (Huge); 4th ghost (2 HD), mummy, shadow, skeleton (Gargantuan), vampire (2 HD), zombie (Gargantuan); 5th ghost (3 HD), skeleton (Colossal), vampire (3 HD), wraith, zombie (Colossal); 6th ghost (4 HD), spectre, vampire (4 HD); 7th ghost (5 HD), mohrg, vampire (5 HD); 8th ghost (6 HD), devourer, vampire (6 HD); 9th ghost (7 HD), nightwing, nightwalker, nightcrawler, vampire (7 HD).
Call Undead VIII.MOD	DESC:As call undead I, except that you call one undead from the 8th-level list, 1d3 of the same kind from the 7th-level list, or 1d4+1 of the same kind from a lower-level list. Call undead list (p.68): 1st skeleton (Tiny, Small or Medium), zombie (Tiny, Small or Medium); 2nd allip, ghoul, skeleton (Large), zombie (Large); 3rd ghast, ghost (1 HD), skeleton (Huge), vampire (1 HD), wight, zombie (Huge); 4th ghost (2 HD), mummy, shadow, skeleton (Gargantuan), vampire (2 HD), zombie (Gargantuan); 5th ghost (3 HD), skeleton (Colossal), vampire (3 HD), wraith, zombie (Colossal); 6th ghost (4 HD), spectre, vampire (4 HD); 7th ghost (5 HD), mohrg, vampire (5 HD); 8th ghost (6 HD), devourer, vampire (6 HD); 9th ghost (7 HD), nightwing, nightwalker, nightcrawler, vampire (7 HD).
Call Undead IX.MOD	DESC:As call undead I, except that you call one undead from the 9th-level list, 1d3 of the same kind from the 8th-level list, or 1d4+1 of the same kind from a lower-level list. Call undead list (p.68): 1st skeleton (Tiny, Small or Medium), zombie (Tiny, Small or Medium); 2nd allip, ghoul, skeleton (Large), zombie (Large); 3rd ghast, ghost (1 HD), skeleton (Huge), vampire (1 HD), wight, zombie (Huge); 4th ghost (2 HD), mummy, shadow, skeleton (Gargantuan), vampire (2 HD), zombie (Gargantuan); 5th ghost (3 HD), skeleton (Colossal), vampire (3 HD), wraith, zombie (Colossal); 6th ghost (4 HD), spectre, vampire (4 HD); 7th ghost (5 HD), mohrg, vampire (5 HD); 8th ghost (6 HD), devourer, vampire (6 HD); 9th ghost (7 HD), nightwing, nightwalker, nightcrawler, vampire (7 HD).
Diamond Body.MOD	DESC:Your body becomes living diamond: damage reduction 15/magic and spell resistance 20; immune to blindness, critical hits, ability score damage, deafness, disease, drowning, electricity, poison, polymorphing, stunning, and anything affecting physiology or respiration; half damage from acid, cold and fire of all kinds; but vulnerable to special attacks that affect constructs. +8 enhancement bonus to Strength, +6 enhancement bonus to Constitution, -4 Dexterity (minimum 1), speed three-quarters normal; arcane spell failure 25%% and armor check penalty -4, as breastplate; you cannot eat or drink (so no potions) or play wind instruments. Your unarmed attacks strike as a mace for your size (1d6 Small, 1d8 Medium) and count as armed. Your weight is multiplied by five, so you sink, but you survive the ocean's depths and lack of air until the spell ends. Arcane material component: a flawless diamond worth at least 5,000 gp. XP cost: 2,000.
Dragon's Blood.MOD	DESC:The subject is unaffected by the frightful presence of one type of dragon (red, white, gold and so on), chosen when cast, and gains a +1 resistance bonus per 5 caster levels (+4 at most, at 20th) on saves against that dragon's spells, spell-like abilities and supernatural abilities. Arcane material component: a scale of that kind of dragon.
Dragonbane.MOD	DESC:Against dragons, the weapon ignores all damage reduction (natural, or from spells, items or supernatural means), its critical multiplier rises by one (x2 becomes x3), and it is unaffected by draconian death throes (a baaz's petrifying corpse, a kapak's acid). Arcane material component: three drops of dragon's blood.
Emotional Brew.MOD	DESC:Infuses liquid (typically alcohol) with an emotion chosen when cast; it takes hold once a full pint is drunk, and the drinker may make a Will save to realize the emotion is not natural. Belligerence: attitude one step worse for 1 hour per pint (Will negates). Depression: -2 morale penalty on saves, attacks, ability checks, skill checks and weapon damage for 1 hour per pint (Will halves); each pint stacks, each hour after the first reducing it by 2 (three pints: -6, then -4, then -2). Fear: panicked, dropping everything and fleeing, -2 morale on saves, skill and ability checks, cowering if cornered, for 1 minute per caster level (Will negates). Friendship: attitude one step better for 1 hour per pint (Will negates). Hope: +2 morale bonus on saves, attacks, ability and skill checks and weapon damage for about 1 hour per pint (Will negates; does not stack). Rage: +2 morale bonus to Strength and Constitution, +1 morale on Will saves, -1 AC, fighting heedless of danger, for 1 minute per caster level (Will negates). Afterward a Fortitude save: success leaves the drinker dazzled (-1 on attacks) for 1 minute per caster level; failure, sickened (-2 on attack rolls, saves, skill and ability checks) for 10 minutes per caster level.
Ensnare the Heart.MOD	DESC:As charm person, but the target's attitude becomes helpful and the effect is permanent.
Ethereal Flame.MOD	DESC:A blast of spectral flame. Living creatures lose 1d4 + 1 per 5 caster levels Wisdom (Fortitude half). Undead lose 1d4 + 1 per 5 caster levels Charisma, and undead brought to 0 Charisma or lower are destroyed. Works on corporeal and incorporeal creatures alike; no effect on nonliving creatures that are not undead. Arcane material component: a silver candle blessed by a cleric.
Eternal Repose.MOD	DESC:Encases a corpse in translucent amber: protected as by temporal stasis, untouched by any force, spell or decay, and it cannot be raised, resurrected or contacted while inside. The coffin is 1 inch thick per caster level, with 30 hit points per inch and hardness 15; destroyed, it releases the body to decay normally. Freedom, limited wish, miracle or wish dispels it. Arcane material component: amber holding a preserved insect or other creature.
Fog of Fear.MOD	DESC:A bluish-green fog cloud whose fumes affect living creatures: 3 HD or fewer are panicked (no save); 4 to 6 HD are panicked, or frightened for the duration on a Will save; 7 HD or more are frightened, or shaken on a save. It rolls away from you 10 feet a round along the ground, obscures all sight (darkvision included) beyond 5 feet, sinks into low places, cannot penetrate liquids and cannot be cast underwater. Arcane material component: a shroud from a corpse already buried.
Greed.MOD	DESC:Living creatures in range are enthralled (as the spell) by one physical object chosen when cast, ignoring their surroundings and indifferent to all else; anyone who tries to take it provokes hostility, even between old friends. Creatures with 4 or more HD or Wisdom 16 or higher stay aware and get another save if they see actions they oppose or are driven to act against their alignment.
Mindweb.MOD	DESC:A living creature entering the web makes a Will save or is mentally paralyzed: effective Strength and Dexterity 0, purely mental actions only, and helpless. Each round a Will save frees it for that round, but if it does not leave the area it may be caught again. Arcane material component: a fly trapped in amber.
Mistshackles.MOD	DESC:A heavy mist holds creatures in place. A trapped creature breaks free and moves at half speed with a full-round Strength or Escape Artist check (DC 13 + caster level); one that makes its Reflex save is not held but moves at half speed through the area. Each of your turns it tries again to hold everyone who avoided or escaped it. Arcane material component: a silk handkerchief twisted and tied in small knots.
Part Death's Shroud.MOD	DESC:Ethereal creatures and objects in the area become visible on the Material Plane, outlined in flickering blue, and are treated as manifested (Monster Manual, ghost): attacks against them gain a +1 circumstance bonus, though corporeal attacks still have a 50%% miss chance. While in the area they cannot fully return to the Ethereal Plane (nothing stops them leaving), and they can interact with the Material Plane. Arcane material component: a translucent quartz mirror in a silver frame.
Reshape Metal.MOD	DESC:As stone shape, for metal: forge a weapon, resize armor, make a crude artwork, open or seal a metal door. Fine detail needs 10 or more ranks in a suitable Craft or Profession; a shape with moving parts has a 30%% chance not to work. Arcane material component: a set of artisan's tools.
Reveal the True Form.MOD	DESC:Shapechangers, and creatures under alter self, polymorph, polymorph any object, shapechange or similar transmutations, make a Fortitude save or revert to their natural form. Those forced back take 2d4 temporary Constitution loss and cannot shapeshift (or cast polymorphing magic) until it returns, and are dazed for 1 round.
Second Life.MOD	DESC:A contingency against unexpected death: if the subject is brought to -10 hit points or lower, dies of massive damage, is slain by a death effect (phantasmal killer, finger of death and the like) or dies by other unnatural means, it returns to life at once. It loses one level (or 1 Hit Die) as if energy drained; a 1st-level subject loses 2 Constitution instead (and cannot be raised if that would bring it to 0 or less). Each prepared spell has a 50%% chance of being lost, and a spontaneous caster has a 50%% chance to lose each unused slot. It returns with hit points equal to its current Hit Dice; ability scores at 0 rise to 1; normal poison and disease are cured, magical ones and curses are not; missing parts stay missing. Not for one turned undead or dying of natural causes such as old age; constructs, elementals, outsiders and undead cannot be raised. Material component: quicksilver and at least 5,000 gp of diamond dust in a crystal vial, carried by the subject.
Spear of Divine Might.MOD	DESC:A ranged touch attack with a bolt of divine energy; good creatures are unaffected. An evil target that fails its Will save is slain if living, destroyed if undead, or banished home if a non-good extraplanar creature (unable to return for 24 hours; it saves against the banishment at -4). An evil target that saves takes 6d8 damage, half force and half holy (Will half). A neutral target is not slain but takes 3d8 force damage (Will half). Creatures whose HD exceed your caster level are unaffected.
Spear of Divine Wrath.MOD	DESC:A ranged touch attack with a bolt of divine energy; evil creatures are unaffected. A good target that fails its Will save is slain if living, destroyed if undead, or banished home if a non-evil extraplanar creature (unable to return for 24 hours; it saves against the banishment at -4). A good target that saves takes 6d8 damage, half force and half unholy (Will half). A neutral target is not slain but takes 3d8 force damage (Will half). Creatures whose HD exceed your caster level are unaffected. (The book's text says "spear of divine might" in this entry's neutral clause.)
Spiritual Horde.MOD	DESC:A visible wall of spirits rolls forward from the point you choose to the spell's range. Living creatures within it make a Fortitude save each round or take 1 point of temporary Constitution loss, and are affected by fear unless they make a Will save at -5. It obscures sight (darkvision included) beyond 5 feet: concealment (20%%) within 5 feet, total concealment (50%%) beyond. From the early Fifth Age to the end of the War of Souls, magic other than necromancy fails inside it as in an antimagic field. Material component: a censer of incense ground with dust from five kinds of intelligent undead. XP cost: 5,000.
Spiritward.MOD	DESC:No ethereal or incorporeal creature can enter the area, and nothing inside can use a spell, ability or item that reaches the Ethereal Plane (a bag of holding or portable hole does not work). Astral travel and spells reaching other planes (summon spells, astral projection) work normally. Arcane material component: fragrant oils, grave dust and powdered gold, spread around the area.
Stirge Swarm.MOD	DESC:Summons one swarm of 1d4+4 stirges per 5 caster levels (4 swarms at most), which attack as you direct within range, each swarm staying together; they vanish when the spell ends. Arcane material component: a stirge's proboscis.
Stonesight.MOD	DESC:You see through earth and stone as if it were not there. Metal (building supports, ore veins) blocks it, crystal and mineral deposits show as hazy color, and water blocks it. It does not let you see in darkness, though low-light vision and darkvision work normally. Arcane focus: a perfectly clear quartz crystal.
Trace Magic.MOD	DESC:You see the lingering threads of magic and can follow one back to its source or on to where it goes. Picking out one thread is a Spellcraft check per thread (DC 15 + spell level, or 15 + half the caster level for a nonspell effect). Threads linger by strength (Table 2-4): faint (0-2nd level spells, minor items) 1d6 minutes; moderate (3rd-5th, moderate items) 1d6 x 10 minutes; strong (6th-8th, minor artifacts) 1d6 hours; overwhelming (9th, major artifacts) 1d6 days. Threads ignore terrain, so you may not be able to follow one (into the air, without flight).
